      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To build a compelling case against a strategy of psychological tactics, your evidence should focus on documenting specific shifts in tone, language, and communication patterns that deviate from standard professional norms. You should collect screenshots or copies of these emails highlighting formal phrasing, use of defensive language, or unanswered questions, as well as recording exact times you attempted to request accommodations or feedback. This curated record helps establish a pattern of unilateral decision-making and potential isolation, which are key components in proving a hostile work environment rather than relying on anecdotes. Ultimately, this standardized documentation is what transforms subjective feelings of being pushed out into objective facts that legal counsel can use to substantiate claims of harassment or constructive dismissal.",
      "source": "target",
